<title>USA: Fair weather continues for Brazil coffee belt- WSC.</title>
<headline>Fair weather continues for Brazil coffee belt- WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The continued high pressure system aloft over Brazil's coffee belt should block any significant cold weather from reaching the area, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Monday.</p>
<p>Mostly fair skies were reported in the coffee belt over the weekend. Temperatures remained near to above normal with lows ranging from 52-62 F (11-16 C).</p>
<p>Continued fair skies are expected through Wednesday. Showers may develop in southern areas of the belt on Thursday. Temperatures should average near to above normal for the week. The lowest temperatures through Sunday will remain above 50 F (10 C), according to WSC.</p>
<p>((--New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
